{
"A guest said: This evening I drew up my net and took a fish, big-mouthed and fine-scaled, shaped like the perch of the Sung River. But where are we to get wine?": "ef76748776f0",
"Ah! Alas! I know you! Was it not you who flew crying past me the night before?": "ce5d59bdc125",
"And I too grew silent and sad, solemn and afraid; it was too chilling to stay.": "aabe8361da72",
"Frost and dew had fallen, the trees had shed all their leaves, our shadows lay on the ground; looking up we saw the bright moon, and glancing round we were glad of it, and sang to one another as we walked.": "95cf0475402f",
"How little time had passed — and yet the river and the hills could no longer be recognized!": "30b58c8aa4a4",
"I asked his name; he bent his head and did not answer.": "1a398716cdd3",
"I dreamed of a Taoist in feather robes, moving lightly, who passed below Lin-kao, bowed to me and said: Was the outing at the Red Cliff a pleasant one?": "953a2297d834",
"I gathered up my robe and climbed: trod the sheer rocks, pushed through the tangled growth, crouched on shapes like tigers and leopards, mounted on roots like coiling dragons, pulled myself up to the perilous nest where the falcon roosts, and looked down into the dark palace of the river god.": "72e78ea3570a",
"I let out one long piercing cry; the grass and trees shook, the hills sounded and the valleys answered, the wind rose and the water surged.": "e332ae3f7e3b",
"I opened the door and looked for him, but could not see where he was.": "a63a0f5db906",
"I turned back and got into the boat, let it drift to midstream, and let it stop wherever it would.": "87886734f062",
"I went home and consulted my wife. She said: I have a measure of wine, long stored away, kept against just such a need of yours.": "5c2c83458af8",
"In a little while the guests left, and I went to sleep.": "07d6f8c2dff7",
"It was near midnight; all around was empty and still.": "556f5620c6fa",
"Just then a solitary crane came across the river from the east, its wings like cartwheels, black skirt and white coat; it gave one harsh long cry, brushed past my boat and went west.": "0b9bd044c86e",
"My two guests could not follow.": "e15ef74fbc14",
"Presently I sighed and said: Here are guests but no wine; and had we wine, there would be no food. The moon is white and the wind is clear — what are we to do with a night like this?": "2a1891405627",
"So, taking the wine and the fish, we went again below the Red Cliff.": "c6066bb2b65e",
"That same year, on the full moon of the tenth month, I walked out from the Snow Hall, meaning to return to Lin-kao.": "b453c97c050c",
"The Taoist looked round and smiled; and I woke with a start.": "bdae4586308a",
"The river ran with a sound; the broken bank stood a thousand feet; the hills were high and the moon small; the water had dropped and the stones stood out.": "e33165612d91",
"Two guests came with me, and we passed the slope of Yellow Mud.": "5d9fb8e91057"
